# SPA fallback for the client-routed gallery.
#
# The gallery is a single-page app, so a deep link such as /runs/<id> has no file
# behind it. This rule REWRITES those requests to the app shell (status 200, not a
# redirect): the shell is served at the original URL, the router resolves the route
# client-side, and the address bar never changes.
#
# The 200 is the point. It replaces a `public/404.html` that stashed the requested
# path in sessionStorage and bounced through `/` to restore it — a workaround for
# GitHub Pages, which has no rewrite configuration at all, carried over unnoticed
# when the gallery moved to Cloudflare Pages. That trick cost a visible flash, and
# it served every run page to crawlers as an HTTP 404 with no markup, so a shared
# or indexed run link resolved to an error. A rewrite fixes both.
#
# Cloudflare Pages matches existing static assets before applying these rules, so
# the per-run assets the build emits (/runs/<id>.json, /run-events/<id>.json) are
# still served as themselves rather than being swallowed by the wildcard.
/*    /index.html    200
